---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How much does a website cost?",
    a: "£50 a month. That covers a custom website for your business, hosting and maintenance, up to 90 minutes of content updates a month, Google Business Profile management and a check-in every two weeks. Your first £50 is paid when you sign up and covers your first month. After that, payments are taken monthly by Direct Debit.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a minimum contract?",
    a: "Yes: a 12-month minimum with an early-exit option. After 12 months, the plan carries on at £50 a month until you cancel. It's an ongoing service, so payments don't stop on their own after 12 months, and paying monthly doesn't make the website yours.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I leave during the first 12 months?",
    a: "Yes, in one of two ways. You can pay £100 to cancel: your monthly payments stop and the website goes offline, but you keep your domain, photos, text and logo. Or you can pay £499 to buy the website: I hand it over to you to keep, and my monthly services stop. Either payment replaces your remaining monthly payments.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I cancel after the first 12 months?",
    a: "Give me 30 days' notice in writing (email is fine). There's no cancellation fee. Unless you buy the website, it goes offline when the plan ends. Before that, I'll send you copies of your content and help you move your domain.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I own my website outright?",
    a: "Yes, for a one-off £499, at any time. I transfer the website's design, code and files to you, and keep it online while you move it to your own hosting. After that, hosting, updates and domain renewal are up to you.",
  },
  {
    q: "What counts as a content update?",
    a: "Changes to your existing pages, like text, prices, opening hours, photos, contact details or a small new section. You get up to 90 minutes a month, and I'll make ordinary changes within 7 days of having everything I need. New pages, new features or a redesign are quoted separately and only go ahead if you agree.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does Google Business Profile management include?",
    a: "You stay the owner and add me as a manager, so I never need your password. I keep your hours, services and details accurate, and aim for 2–4 useful posts a month, depending on what's going on in your business and what photos and news you can share. I won't post filler or invent offers, and I can't promise rankings or a number of enquiries.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do the check-ins work?",
    a: "Every two weeks you'll get a message by email or WhatsApp with a link to a short form. Use it to tell me about anything that needs changing. You can also use the form between check-ins whenever something comes up.",
  },
  {
    q: "Who owns my domain and content?",
    a: "You do, whatever happens. If you already have a domain, you keep it. If you need a new one, I'll register it in your name and cover the standard yearly cost within an agreed allowance while you're on the plan. If you leave, the domain is still yours and you take over renewing it.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long does a website take?",
    a: "It varies by project, but most websites are ready within a few weeks of getting started, depending on how quickly content and feedback come together.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can you redesign my existing website?",
    a: "Yes. Redesigns are one of the most common projects — bringing an outdated or hard-to-use website up to a modern, mobile-friendly standard.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to provide the written content?",
    a: "Ideally yes, since you know your business best, but I'll guide you on what's needed and can help shape and tidy up the wording where it helps.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is included in the free homepage preview?",
    a: "A first look at how your homepage could feel and read, based on the information you share. There's no cost and no obligation to continue afterwards.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will the website work properly on mobile?",
    a: "Yes. Every Stapled. website is built mobile-first and tested across different screen sizes, since most local customers will find you on their phone.",
  },
];
---

<section class="faq section" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq__inner">
    <div class="faq__intro reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="faq__heading">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq__list reveal">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="faq__item">
          <summary>
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-muted">{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq__inner {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .faq__intro {
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .faq__heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
  }

  .faq__item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq__item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq__item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq__chevron {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .faq__item[open] .faq__chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq__item p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-right: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .faq__item p {
      animation: faq-in var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
    }
  }

  @keyframes faq-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(-4px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }
</style>
